                    {
                        "sense_id": "bacdca5c-e42c-3d9a-9388-2696ddc58fe0",
                        "entry_id": "8c342776-506a-30ca-80a9-77708f05c22d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To spread over or across (something); cover over; be scattered over; permeate, overrun."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa5d6353-8f02-4aee-a913-9dcb38289614",
                                "sense_id": "bacdca5c-e42c-3d9a-9388-2696ddc58fe0",
                                "text": "those nations of the North which overspread the world"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "77422eea-f3ab-4b92-b581-d744c3ee800b",
                                "sense_id": "bacdca5c-e42c-3d9a-9388-2696ddc58fe0",
                                "text": "Lady Bellaston fixed her eyes on Sophia whilst she spoke these words. To which that poor young lady, having her face overspread with blushes and confusion, answered, in a stammering voice […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "818d41cf-4ec2-497b-b6d4-0c75afa87fa3",
                                "sense_id": "bacdca5c-e42c-3d9a-9388-2696ddc58fe0",
                                "text": "So thick a haze o’erspreads the sky,\nThey cannot see the sun on high:\nThe wind hath blown a gale all day;\nAt evening it hath died away."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "798fc85e-a832-4b7b-8f5d-9de5f82c5ed9",
                                "sense_id": "bacdca5c-e42c-3d9a-9388-2696ddc58fe0",
                                "text": "Deliberately, and with a peculiar quivering smile, that seemed to overspread her whole body, she put her mouth on his."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "22b9d767-196a-36a8-9b77-d1dabc148c14",
                        "entry_id": "8c342776-506a-30ca-80a9-77708f05c22d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To be spread or scattered about."
                        ],
